{"agent":"dx-round-justified","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The rule first says a plain review runs when the item’s reviewed paths “differ now,” then says “A merge of main … is not new work.” That is wrong for a merge that changes one of the item’s reviewed files. Example: the last round recorded `src/foo.py`; the branch is then merged with main, and the merge resolves a conflict in `src/foo.py`. The tree at that reviewed path differs now, so the change should be new work, but the doc classifies the merge as not new work and would skip a reviewer. The exception must be limited to merges that do not touch any reviewed path.","digest":"4db3f4032c7b5018","location":"ddflow/config_sections/review.py review.require_new_work doc","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/config_sections/review.py review.require_new_work doc"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`test_full_and_the_knob_still_run_a_round` first calls `api.review(..., full=True)`, which re-runs the critic gate and records new untriaged findings. The subsequent `_plain` is then already justified by the “untriaged finding” branch, so the assertion passes even if `[review].require_new_work = false` is ignored or removed. This test does not actually verify the knob it claims to cover and gives false confidence in the new `require_new_work` behavior.","digest":"e88a0ef2ee6ea0ee","location":"tests/test_review_round_justified.py:66-71","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_review_round_justified.py:66-71"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12508,"diff_sha":"db88a6374bded40fd2bbf2979bc5554c52813f737afcfa8e78fc54699ae635aa","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":932.7,"excluded_bytes":1186751,"excluded_files":3,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_outputs.ambr","tests/te